Sage Windows Unified Engine

Original integration and host scheduling code is distributed under Apache-2.0.

The selected RMSNorm kernel derives from NInfer by Neroued and the loktoto
SM75 fork, under Apache-2.0. See kernels/ for exact source attribution and changes.

PolyStrata/Strata and its dependencies retain their own licenses in the pinned
source checkout. Build/package distributors must include those license files.
The integration patches do not replace the licenses of patched upstream files.

The separately pinned Turing-unlock-windows project is GPL-2.0-only research
input. Its source is not included in or linked into this inference runtime.

Sage-A1.5 model weights are separate artifacts. Their publisher's model license
and notices apply; no model weights are redistributed in this repository.

The GGUF Q6_K byte decoder is adapted from iamwavecut/ninfer-all,
commit 71d3f8190772ef7089f8eda4e22371114fd5bbf9, under Apache-2.0.
Its block layout follows ggml Q6_K; source and numerical details are recorded
in docs/Q6K_DONOR.md.


The IQ4_XS decoder and two-row warp vector schedule are adapted from
iamwavecut/ninfer-all, commit 71d3f8190772ef7089f8eda4e22371114fd5bbf9,
under Apache-2.0. The adapter uses Strata's interleaved Q8_1 slots.
